-- הודעת תכ"ם HOD.13.4.2.1 "לוח תעריפי נסיעה בתחבורה ציבורית", מהדורה 17
-- (2.3.2023). Edition 16's text, with its one change (its table of
-- changes): trips on duty are refunded only where the employee must go out
-- of the city of home or work; the calculator takes addresses.
-- Its tables are DATA here, written by tools/tariff_l4.py from the corpus
-- and held to it by tests/test_tariffs.py.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT parties
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT `kitzuvat-nesia-common`
IMPORT `taarifei-nesia-common`

-- not weighed against `the Wage Protection Law`: the notice sets the
-- tariffs by which a travel EXPENSE is refunded (‘החזר בגין הוצאות’) and
-- the supplement that softens its cut, not wages.

§ `הודעת תכ"ם 13.4.2.1 לוח תעריפי נסיעה בתחבורה ציבורית — מהדורה 17`

`notice 17 is published` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2023

§§ `1 רקע ומטרה`

-- 1.1 and 1.3: from 1.8.2022 the tariffs differ by the distance between
-- origin and destination and by the means (bus, or bus and train), as the
-- summary table of 1.3 prints them, with the single trips by bus or by train.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-1 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3
`the reform notice 17 applies from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2022

-- tariff data akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3/t1 (tools/tariff_l4.py)
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3/t1
`notice 17's fare table 1` MEANS
    `a fare table` ""
        (LIST `a fare column` (JUST `a daily free pass`) (JUST `bus and train`) NOTHING, `a fare column` (JUST `a monthly free pass`) (JUST `bus and train`) NOTHING, `a fare column` (JUST `a single trip`) (JUST `bus only`) NOTHING, `a fare column` (JUST `a single trip`) (JUST `train only`) NOTHING)
        (LIST `ranged` 0 (JUST 15) (LIST (JUST 18), (JUST 255), (JUST 5.5), (JUST 9)),
              `ranged` 15 (JUST 40) (LIST (JUST 28), (JUST 255), (JUST 12), (JUST 18)),
              `ranged` 40 (JUST 75) (LIST (JUST 37), (JUST 410), (JUST 16), (JUST 24)),
              `ranged` 75 (JUST 120) (LIST (JUST 42), (JUST 610), (JUST 16), (JUST 27)),
              `ranged` 120 (JUST 225) (LIST (JUST 74), (JUST 610), (JUST 27), (JUST 48)),
              `ranged` 255 NOTHING (LIST NOTHING, (JUST 610), (JUST 68.5), NOTHING))

-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-2 A pointer to the Ministry of Transport's page on the reform; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-4 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-5 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-5/p2 The agreement to soften the cut for existing employees (its rules are 2.2) and the notice's purpose; no rule.

§§ `2.1 כללי`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1 The heading "כללי"; its clauses follow.

-- 2.1.1 and 2.1.3: the refund is the relevant tariff, by the code reported
-- for the distance between the addresses of home and work as the Derech
-- Shava calculator gives it: the monthly free pass "אוטובוס + רכבת" of the
-- distance band (1.3); some employees are paid the equalisation supplement
-- besides (2.2). The calculator is outside the corpus: the distance is the
-- input.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-3
`the card notice 17 pays by` MEANS `bus and train`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-3
GIVEN km IS A NUMBER @desc the distance between home and work the calculator gives
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `notice 17's monthly allowance for the distance` km IS
    `the fare for the distance` `notice 17's fares` km `a monthly free pass` `the card notice 17 pays by`

-- 2.1.2: the salary accountant enters the calculator, gets the route's
-- tariffs, and reports the symbol with the tariff code (4.2).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tariff-notice duty`
DECIDE `finding and reporting the code, notice 17` IS
    PARTY `the salary accountant`
    MUST  `find the route's tariff code or distance on the Ministry of Transport's calculator`
    HENCE (PARTY `the salary accountant`
           MUST  `report the route's tariff code in the payroll`)

§§ `2.2 עובדים קיימים`

-- 2.2 and annex A: an existing employee is a MONTHLY employee employed in a
-- ministry or an auxiliary unit on 31.7.2022; so is one employed that day
-- whose employment was broken afterwards for up to 6 months and resumed, or
-- who moved to another ministry or auxiliary unit, or home. A new employee
-- is one taken in from 1.8.2022, save those. The supplement is paid to
-- existing monthly employees alone, an hourly employee being entitled to
-- none (2.2/p2, 2.2.5).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2/p2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-5 akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_2
GIVEN `a monthly employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `employed on 31.7.2022` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months the employment was broken since` IS A NUMBER @desc 0 where it never was
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `owed the equalisation supplement under notice 17` `a monthly employee` `employed on 31.7.2022` `months the employment was broken since` IF
    `a monthly employee` AND `employed on 31.7.2022` AND `months the employment was broken since` AT MOST 6

-- 2.2.1-2.2.3: where the allowance before the reform was below the new
-- tariff, the new tariff is paid (2.2.1); where the reform cut it by less
-- than 60 shekels against the highest of 2022 on the same route, the new
-- tariff, and no supplement (2.2.2); where by more than 60, the supplement
-- by the table: X less the reductions made, and no lower than the row's
-- floor (2.2.3). A cut of exactly 60 is named by neither; the table pays it
-- no supplement either way. 2.2.4: in August of every year a further 60 is
-- cut, up to the row's maximal cumulative reduction.
-- X: 2.2.3 counts "כלל התוספות שניתנו בעקבות רפורמת 2016", and its own
-- definition of X under the table "רפורמת 2018". X is read as the definition
-- under the table defines it (finding F-…v17-b).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-3 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-3/p2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-4
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER @desc the allowance paid before the reform, every component included (the supplements of the 2018 reform with them)
      `the new tariff` IS A NUMBER
      `the highest allowance of 2022` IS A NUMBER @desc on the same route
      d IS A DATE @desc the month's day
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `notice 17's equalisation supplement` x `the new tariff` `the highest allowance of 2022` d IS
    IF `the highest allowance of 2022` MINUS `the new tariff` AT MOST `the cut notice 17 pays no supplement for`
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE `the equalisation supplement by the table` `notice 17's equalisation table` x `the new tariff` (`the reductions notice 17 has made by` d)

`the cut notice 17 pays no supplement for` MEANS 60

-- The first reduction is the reform's own, from 1.8.2022; each August
-- after it, another.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-4
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the reductions notice 17 has made by` d IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2022) THEN 0
        IF DATE_MONTH d AT LEAST 8 THEN DATE_YEAR d MINUS 2021
        OTHERWISE DATE_YEAR d MINUS 2022

-- tariff data akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-3/t1 (tools/tariff_l4.py)
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-3/t1
`notice 17's equalisation table` MEANS
    LIST `an equalisation row` 1450 NOTHING (JUST 350) (JUST 1100) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 1300 (JUST 1450) (JUST 340) (JUST 980) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 1150 (JUST 1300) (JUST 320) (JUST 850) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 1000 (JUST 1150) (JUST 300) (JUST 730) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 850 (JUST 1000) (JUST 270) (JUST 610) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 750 (JUST 850) (JUST 240) (JUST 550) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 650 (JUST 750) (JUST 200) (JUST 490) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 550 (JUST 650) (JUST 160) (JUST 430) (JUST 60),
         `an equalisation row` 0 (JUST 550) (JUST 120) NOTHING (JUST 60)

-- What 2.2.3 counts in the cut, and what its definition of X counts.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-3 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-3/p2
`the reform whose supplements notice 17's 2.2.3 counts` MEANS 2016
`the reform whose supplements notice 17's X counts` MEANS 2018
`notice 17 counts the supplements of two reforms in X` MEANS
    NOT `the reform whose supplements notice 17's 2.2.3 counts` EQUALS `the reform whose supplements notice 17's X counts`
#ASSERT `notice 17 counts the supplements of two reforms in X`

§§ `2.3 שינוי כתובת מגורים לעובדים קיימים`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.3.1: the employee must tell human resources of a new address or
-- workplace; a move farther away keeps the supplement of 1.8.2022 without
-- recalculation (2.3.1.1); a move nearer leaves the new tariffs alone, no
-- supplement (2.3.1.2).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `reporting a move, notice 17` IS
    PARTY `the government employee`
    MUST  `report the new address or workplace on the travel-allowance form`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-1__pnt_2-3-1-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-1__pnt_2-3-1-2
GIVEN `the supplement of 1.8.2022` IS A NUMBER
      `the move is nearer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc by the reform's distance bands
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `notice 17's supplement after a move` `the supplement of 1.8.2022` `the move is nearer` IS
    IF `the move is nearer` THEN 0 ELSE `the supplement of 1.8.2022`

§§ `3 נסיעות בתפקיד`

-- 3.1: trips on duty are refunded only where the employee must go out of the city of home or work, at the daily free pass of the means used ("חופשי יומי –
-- אוטובוס" or "– אוטובוס + רכבת"): up to 1,000 shekels a month to an
-- employee with a service car (3.1.1), up to 1,500 to one with no car
-- standard, on report (3.1.2). 3.2: reported under symbol 1247.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-1 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-1__cls_3-1-1 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-1__cls_3-1-2
GIVEN `the daily passes of the trips on duty` IS A NUMBER
      `has a service car` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `notice 17's refund for trips on duty` `the daily passes of the trips on duty` `has a service car` IS
    min `the daily passes of the trips on duty` (IF `has a service car` THEN 1000 ELSE 1500)

@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tariff-notice duty`
DECIDE `reporting trips on duty, notice 17` IS
    PARTY `the salary accountant`
    MUST  `report the single trips on duty`

§§ `4 אופן הדיווח`

-- akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-1 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-2 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-3 The headings of the two stages; their clauses follow.

-- 4.1-4.3: the distance band is taken from the Ministry's calculator (it
-- shows the distance only), the monthly free pass of the band read from
-- the table of 1.3, the symbol and event as the instruction 13.4.2 says, and
-- the tariff code in event 226. 4.3.2 says the codes "start at 1011"; the
-- table of 4.4 prints them 1110 to 1160, and the code reported is the
-- table's.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-1__cls_4-1-1 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-1__cls_4-1-2 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-2__cls_4-2-1 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-2__cls_4-2-1__pnt_4-2-1-1 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-2__cls_4-2-1__pnt_4-2-1-2 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-2__cls_4-2-1__pnt_4-2-1-3 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-2__cls_4-2-1__pnt_4-2-1-4 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-3__cls_4-3-1 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-3__cls_4-3-2 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-4
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tariff-notice duty`
DECIDE `reporting the code in Malam, notice 17` IS
    PARTY `the salary accountant`
    MUST  `find the route's tariff code or distance on the Ministry of Transport's calculator`
    HENCE (PARTY `the salary accountant`
           MUST  `report the route's tariff code in the payroll`)

